  Joint frames, position and velocity limits, the gripper_frame_link TCP and
  each part's collision element are upstream's; each collision mesh is the
  convex hull of the part's upstream mesh, under meshes/. gripper_link also
  carries the wrist camera module: the hull of the camera mount and the
  camera on it, in the link's frame. robot_description/tools/so101_collision_hulls.py
  writes every mesh.

  Physical corrections:
  - The effort limit of each joint is 2.94 N*m, the stall torque of the
    follower's servo, where upstream gives 10. Each joint is driven by one
    Feetech STS3215, the sts3215_03a part on its parent link; the 12 V
    STS3215 stalls at 30 kg*cm (robotshop.com/products/feetech-12v-30kgcm-magnetic-encoding-servo-sts3215),
    30 * 9.80665 / 100 = 2.942 N*m, and MuJoCo Menagerie's
    robotstudio_so101 gives its sts3215 actuators forcerange 2.94.
-->
